<!--
  <sui-field> — SUI port of <ship-field>.
  Vertical stack: label slot → control slot → hint/error. Wires
  aria-describedby from the first slotted control to the hint/error
  div, and sets invalid on the control to match the field's state.

  Prop / event / method parity vs <ship-field>
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Lit                            SUI                       Notes
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  invalid (Boolean, false)       invalid (bool, false,     ✓
                                   reflect)
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Slots: label, (default),       label, (default),         ✓ hint/error swap via
    hint, error                    hint, error               CSS; both always in DOM
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  ARIA: aria-describedby wired   ✓ controller wires refs   ✓
    from slotted control to        to slotted control
    hint/error div id
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  NEW SURFACE (re-port from the feat/next baseline, parity-gate pass)
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  - Dropped the bare `[hidden]: display:none` host variant — the framework's
    global BASE_CSS now ships `:host([hidden]) { display: none !important; }`
    for every shadow component (adoptSuiSheets), so a per-component copy is
    dead weight (same principle as the tone/size channels, generalized to
    the hidden-visibility reset).
  - The hint/error visibility toggle STAYS hand-authored CSS in the residual
    style block (unlike alert's dismiss-visibility, which moved to a variants
    block) — see the two LANG-GAPs below.

  LANG-GAP — hint/error show/hide isn't reachable via variants at all
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Tried moving this to `<variants class="error">`/`<variants class="hint">`
  first (the anatomy-class convention alert established) and hit two closed-
  vocabulary walls stacked on top of each other:
  1. The variants attribute-selector grammar has no negation (attr_match in
     crates/sui/compiler/src/parse/preprocess.rs accepts only a bare
     identifier or an [attr] literal) — a `:not([invalid])` selector line
     silently lowers to nothing, no compile error, no test failure.
  2. Even routed around that (flip the base to hidden, use one positive
     `[invalid]: display:flex` line instead of a negated pair), `display`'s sx
     vocabulary (Kind::Display in crates/sui/lint/src/rules/sx.rs) only
     offers block/inline/inline-block/inline-flex/none — plain `flex` isn't a
     legal token, so that line ALSO silently lowers to nothing.
  Both failures are silent (no diagnostic), which is the real hazard: nothing
  short of inspecting the compiled `styles:` string surfaces them, and this
  vitest suite never checks computed style. Reverted to hand-authored CSS
  (below), which supports :not() and `flex` natively — exactly feat/next's
  own two rules, unchanged.

  BUGFIX found in the pass: the pre-existing spike's error-visibility variant
  attempt (since reverted, per the LANG-GAP above) was inverted — it read
  `[invalid]: display:none` plus a `:not([invalid]): display:flex` line
  combined with an unconditional `.error { display:flex }` style-block base.
  Since the negated line always silently vanished (LANG-GAP #1), only
  `:host([invalid]) .error {display:none}` survived — and its higher
  specificity than the plain `.error {display:flex}` base meant it always
  won, hiding the error exactly when it should show and showing it exactly
  when it shouldn't. No test caught it because none of the vitest assertions
  check computed style, only DOM structure/attributes.
-->

<prop name="invalid" type="bool" default="false" reflect />

<!-- Residual: the host flex column layout (no layout primitive for the
     vertical stack of label + control + hint/error); .msg/.hint/.error
     typography + the .hint margin-top; the .error row geometry
     (align-items:flex-start doesn't fit <row align=>'s start/center/
     end/stretch/baseline enum, and the error row needs the specific
     flex-start alignment for icon alignment); the inline SVG icon
     (width/height/flex-shrink); the hint/error visibility toggle (the two
     LANG-GAPs above — no negation and no plain `flex` in the variants/sx
     vocabulary). -->
<style>
  :host {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-1);
  }
  .msg { margin-top: var(--space-1); }
  .hint,
  .error {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
  }
  .hint { color: var(--muted-foreground); }
  .error {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--space-1);
    color: var(--destructive);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-medium);
  }
  .error svg { width: var(--icon-size-sm); height: var(--icon-size-sm); flex-shrink: 0; }

  :host(:not([invalid])) .error { display: none; }
  :host([invalid]) .hint { display: none; }
</style>

<slot name="label"></slot>
<slot bind:this={controlSlot}></slot>
<div class="hint msg" part="hint" bind:this={hintEl}><slot name="hint"></slot></div>
<div class="error msg" part="error" role="alert" aria-live="polite" bind:this={errorEl}>
  <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M10.3 3.9 1.8 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.7 3h17a2 2 0 0 0 1.7-3L13.7 3.9a2 2 0 0 0-3.4 0z"></path><path d="M12 9v4M12 17h.01"></path></svg>
  <span><slot name="error"></slot></span>
</div>
